    "font" : "TeXGyreTermesX-Regular",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The above substitution emphasizes the fact that we are now dealing directly with the exponential distribution of the squared magnitudes \uD835\uDC4B1 and \uD835\uDC4B2, rather than with the complex fields \uD835\uDC4D1 and \uD835\uDC4D2 because \uD835\uDF0E2 and \uD835\uDF0C are, respectively, the variance and the correlation coefficient of \uD835\uDC4B1 and \uD835\uDC4B2, as shown in the previous section. We now seek to extend this result to the sum of \uD835\uDC58 independent correlated exponential variables, leading to correlated Gamma-distributed variables."
  }, {
